{
  "rationale": "The plant models robot perception and motion as separate automata, with all sensor outcomes and motion commands as events. The specification enforces conservative exploration: random_walk is used in clear/search states, move_forward is only allowed in a short forward_commit state, and all obstacle events force deterministic turn-based recovery before returning to exploration. No forward or random_walk is allowed in obstacle states. The design ensures steady progress, reliable avoidance, and no infinite forward or recovery loops.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion to reflect the robot's sensing and actuation subsystems.",
    "Specification automaton binds sensor outcomes to safe, conservative actions, enforcing recovery after obstacles and alternating exploration actions."
  ],
